  {
   "id": "text94",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 978,
   "y": 1041,
   "width": 423.0,
   "height": 281.25,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 858641202,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 2116481899,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Open decisions that change these ports\n\n1. Weights from SRAM, or streamed?\n   -> keep or drop the memory-manager group\n2. Block scaling (slides: TBD)\n   -> scale streams ws_* stay, change or go\n3. Address units: today fp32-element addresses.\n   INT4/8/16 data in SRAM needs byte addresses\n   and byte write masks\n4. Read bandwidth: OUTER reads S, k and \u0394;\n   GEMV reads A and x -> NRdPorts\n5. Saturation: an error (err_code_o) or a\n   sticky flag (flag_sat_o)?\n6. Command encoding belongs to control/ISA;\n   mat_cmd_t is our proposal to them",
   "originalText": "Open decisions that change these ports\n\n1. Weights from SRAM, or streamed?\n   -> keep or drop the memory-manager group\n2. Block scaling (slides: TBD)\n   -> scale streams ws_* stay, change or go\n3. Address units: today fp32-element addresses.\n   INT4/8/16 data in SRAM needs byte addresses\n   and byte write masks\n4. Read bandwidth: OUTER reads S, k and \u0394;\n   GEMV reads A and x -> NRdPorts\n5. Saturation: an error (err_code_o) or a\n   sticky flag (flag_sat_o)?\n6. Command encoding belongs to control/ISA;\n   mat_cmd_t is our proposal to them",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
